export PATH=/opt/alt/alt-nodejs22/root/usr/bin:$PATH

chmod -R u+rwX node_modules
chmod +x node_modules/.bin/vite

npm run build

The fix

This is the command you want to remember:

chmod 755 /home/sixonici/dus.sixonicit.com

Then verify:

ls -ld /home/sixonici/dus.sixonicit.com

Great! Your build completed successfully. Now you need to complete the deployment process. Here's what to do next:

## 1. Clear and Cache Everything

```bash
# Clear all caches
php artisan optimize:clear

# Or individually:
php artisan cache:clear
php artisan config:clear
php artisan view:clear
php artisan route:clear
php artisan event:clear
php artisan clear-compiled
```

## 2. Cache for Production

```bash
# Cache configurations for production
php artisan config:cache
php artisan route:cache
php artisan view:cache
php artisan event:cache

# Or use optimize (combines all caches)
php artisan optimize
```

## 3. Run Database Migrations (if any)

```bash
# Check if there are pending migrations
php artisan migrate --pretend

# If there are migrations, run them
php artisan migrate --force

# Or if you need to seed
php artisan db:seed --force
```

## 4. Set Proper Permissions

```bash
# Set proper permissions for storage and bootstrap/cache
chmod -R 775 storage
chmod -R 775 bootstrap/cache
chmod -R 775 public/build

# Set ownership (adjust user:group as needed)
chown -R $(whoami):$(whoami) storage
chown -R $(whoami):$(whoami) bootstrap/cache
```

## 5. Bring Site Back Online

```bash
# Bring the application out of maintenance mode
php artisan up
```

## 6. Verify Everything is Working

```bash
# Check PHP version
php -v

# Check installed packages
composer show

# Check routes
php artisan route:list

# Test the application
curl -I https://dus.sixonicit.com
```

## Complete Command Sequence

Here's the complete sequence to run:

```bash
# 1. Clear all caches
php artisan optimize:clear

# 2. Cache for production
php artisan config:cache
php artisan route:cache
php artisan view:cache
php artisan event:cache

# 3. Run migrations if needed
php artisan migrate --force

# 4. Set permissions
chmod -R 775 storage bootstrap/cache public/build

# 5. Bring site back online
php artisan up

# 6. Check if site is accessible
curl -I https://dus.sixonicit.com
```

## Additional Checks

### Check the Maintenance Page
Visit your site to see the custom maintenance page you created:

```
https://dus.sixonicit.com
```

### Verify the Build Files

```bash
# Check if build files exist
ls -la public/build/assets/

# Check if the maintenance view was created
ls -la resources/views/errors/maintenance.blade.php
```

### Check for Errors in Logs

```bash
# Check Laravel logs
tail -f storage/logs/laravel.log

# Check PHP error logs
tail -f /path/to/php-error.log
```

## Troubleshooting

### If the site still shows maintenance mode:

```bash
# Force remove maintenance mode
rm -f storage/framework/down

# Or
php artisan up --force
```

### If you see 500 errors:

```bash
# Check the logs
cat storage/logs/laravel.log

# Check file permissions
ls -la storage/framework/cache/
ls -la storage/framework/views/
ls -la bootstrap/cache/
```

### If assets are not loading:

```bash
# Rebuild assets
npm run build

# Or clear Vite cache
rm -rf node_modules/.vite
npm run build
```

### If you need to rollback:

```bash
# Put site back in maintenance mode
php artisan down

# Rollback the last deployment
git reset --hard HEAD~1

# Clear caches
php artisan optimize:clear

# Rebuild assets
npm run build

# Bring site back up
php artisan up
```

## Quick Reference Card

```bash
# === DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST ===

# 1. Build completed ✓
npm run build  # Already done

# 2. Clear and cache
php artisan optimize:clear
php artisan config:cache
php artisan route:cache
php artisan view:cache

# 3. Migrate (if needed)
php artisan migrate --force

# 4. Permissions
chmod -R 775 storage bootstrap/cache public/build

# 5. Bring online
php artisan up

# 6. Verify
curl -I https://dus.sixonicit.com
```

## Monitor After Deployment

```bash
# Watch logs in real-time
tail -f storage/logs/laravel.log

# Check server status
top -u $(whoami)

# Check disk space
df -h
```

Once you've run these commands, your site should be live with the custom maintenance page showing when you're in maintenance mode, and the BackToTop and CookieConsent features working correctly.